  "summary": "Duplicate Advisory: PYTHON-6110 Out-of-bounds read in BSON decoding via a malformed Regex element",
  "details": "## Duplicate Advisory\n\nThis advisory has been withdrawn because it is a duplicate of GHSA-98qm-wvgf-w4cf. This link is maintained to preserve external references.\n\n## Original Description\nThe MongoDB Python Driver's binary accelerator can read outside a buffer when an application decodes malformed BSON containing a truncated regular-expression element without a trailing NUL byte. An actor who can supply BSON to the documented decode or decode_all API can cause the application process to terminate when the C extension is loaded. The driver's normal database wire-protocol path does not reach this code.",
